      "message": "You can save a multiply if you use bit twiddling.\nFor the 32 bit case:\n\nbitcast\u003cf32\u003e( bitcast\u003cu32\u003e(N) xor \n              ((bitcast\u003cu32\u003e(Nref) xor bitcast\u003cu32\u003e(I) xor u32(-1)) \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 31))\n              \n              \nBut that\u0027s way less readable.   I don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth saving the multiply.  The depth of the pipeline is probably more important.",
